<title>FRANCE: Alcatel details telecoms market outlook.</title>
<headline>Alcatel details telecoms market outlook.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel Alsthom gave the following forecasts for market growth in the world number of users of fixed telecoms lines, mobile telecoms subscribers and Internet users, in millions.</p>
<p>    YEAR		   1996     1997    1998   1999   2000</p>
<p>    Fixed lines	   715	760     820    875    940</p>
<p>    Mobile subscribers  130	201     275    351    425</p>
<p>    Internet users	 35	 75     120    180    250</p>
<p>It gave the following forecasts, in billions of dollars, of the growth in the world telecoms market by segment.</p>
<p>    YEAR				   1996		2000</p>
<p>    public switches		     26.5	     26.9</p>
<p>    transmission			  13.0	     15.8</p>
<p>    access				   8.0	     17.8</p>
<p>    space				    4.6		5.9</p>
<p>    cellular infrastructure	   17.4	     29.7</p>
<p>    PABX and applications	     17.8	     25.9</p>
<p>    data tranmission		    23.7	     28.7</p>
<p>    voice terminals		     38.3	     45.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Alcatel Alsthom gave the figures in handouts during its 1996 results news conference. Chairman Serge Tchuruk said the company aimed to sell three million digital phones in 1997 and become profitable in the activity in 1998.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
